    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# RAG Workflow for Knowledge Base - Addition\n\n## Purpose\nIngests a newly added knowledge-base file into the Pinecone vector store (and downstream PageIndex) so the chatbot can retrieve it. Acts as the canonical 'add' pipeline for both autonomous Drive uploads and other workflows that programmatically push new docs into the KB.\n\n## How it works\n- Accepts two entry points: a Google Drive trigger that watches the Knowledge_Base folder for newly created files, and an Execute-Workflow trigger that lets other workflows pass `fileId` + `fileName` directly\n- Dedupes against previously seen file checksums to avoid re-ingesting the same file\n- Normalizes input field names from either trigger, downloads the file binary from Drive, attaches metadata (fileId, fileName, uploadDate)\n- Splits the document with a recursive character text splitter, embeds chunks with OpenAI embeddings, and inserts them into the Pinecone `company-files` index\n- Logs the addition in the Rag_File_Tracker sheet (status = active) and forwards to the PageIndex addition sub-workflow so PageIndex stays in sync\n\n## Triggered by\n- Google Drive trigger on the `Knowledge_Base` folder (fileCreated, polled every minute)\n- Execute Workflow trigger with `fileId` + `fileName` (called by other workflows)\n\n## Calls (sub-workflows)\n- PageIndex Workflow for Knowledge Base - Addition  mirrors the addition into the PageIndex document store after the vector embedding succeeds.\n\n## Called by\n- Human Cases RAG Updater\n\n## Reads/writes\n- Reads from Google Drive `Knowledge_Base` folder\n- Writes to Pinecone index `company-files` (with OpenAI embeddings)\n- Appends to Google Sheets `Customer_Support_Data`  `Rag_File_Tracker`",
        "height": 850,
        "width": 1100,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky-overview-doc",
      "name": "Workflow Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -704,
        -400
      ]
    }
